# Build context trim for the server image (deploy/compose/Dockerfile.server) and
# the sandbox image (deploy/sandbox/Dockerfile, which copies nothing). The server
# build needs ONLY: pyproject.toml, uv.lock, packages/, scripts/, deploy/. Keep
# everything else out of the daemon context — it's slow, and several of these
# carry local state/secrets that must never land in an image layer.

# --- heavy / irrelevant ---
.git
.venv
frontend            # built by its own frontend/Dockerfile
node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- local runtime state + SECRETS (never ship these) ---
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
disco-config.json
secrets.json
*secret*
.env
.env.*

# --- developer scratch / harness / captured runs (not needed at runtime) ---
.orchestrate
agent-projects
test-record
review-queue
bakeoff
harness
evals
prompts
run_manual*.py
test_*.py
*.csv
validation_output.txt
validate.py

# --- docs (the image doesn't serve them) ---
*.md
docs
